# Next.js 16.2 — what differs from training data

This project runs Next.js **16.2.10** / React **19.2.4**, App Router, TypeScript strict.
The points below are the changes that actually affect this codebase. If you need an
API that is *not* covered here, read the matching file under
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing code — but grep it first with
`rg --no-ignore` (that tree is gitignored, so ripgrep skips it by default) and read
only the relevant section. Several of those docs are 40–60 KB.

## Async request APIs

Synchronous access is fully removed in 16 — `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()`,
`headers()` and `draftMode()` are all Promises.

```tsx
export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params;
}
```

`npx next typegen` generates `PageProps<'/admin/ordens/[id]'>`, `LayoutProps` and
`RouteContext` helpers if you prefer typed route params over hand-written shapes.

## Caching and invalidation

`unstable_cache` is still named `unstable_cache` — do not "fix" it. It wraps the
read side in `src/lib/data.ts`.

For the write side, **always invalidate through the `invalidateCache()` helper in
`src/lib/cache-tags.ts`** and use a tag from the `CACHE_TAGS` registry rather than a
string literal. Bare `revalidateTag(tag)` is deprecated in 16 and is a TypeScript
error: it now takes a second argument (a `cacheLife` profile such as `'max'`, or an
options object). The helper passes `{ expire: 0 }` so writes are visible on the very
next read, which matters because some call sites (e.g. the machine ingest route
handler) are not Server Actions.

Also available in 16, both Server-Action-only: `updateTag(tag)` for read-your-writes
semantics, and `refresh()` to refresh the client router. Prefer the existing
`invalidateCache()` + `revalidatePath()` pattern for consistency unless you have a
specific reason.

`cacheLife` and `cacheTag` are now stable — import them without the `unstable_`
prefix. `experimental.dynamicIO` and `experimental.useCache` were removed.

## Routing

`middleware.ts` is now **`proxy.ts`** — this project has `src/proxy.ts`, which
re-exports the Auth.js handler and a route `matcher`. Do not create a `middleware.ts`.

Parallel routes now require a `default.js`. `next/image` dropped
`images.domains` in favour of `remotePatterns`.

## Tooling

Turbopack is the default for `next dev` and `next build`. The `next lint` command was
removed: the `lint` script calls `eslint` directly, with flat config in
`eslint.config.mjs`.
